WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.274 --> 00:00:17.342
As soon as I finished my muffin, I went across the hall to Molly's apartment.

2
00:00:18.983 --> 00:00:24.145
Molly came to the door wearing her purple bathrobe and eating a chocolate-covered donut.

3
00:00:24.166 --> 00:00:28.128
"I'm having a mental health day," Molly announced.

4
00:00:29.804 --> 00:00:32.145
Tate had told me all about mental health days.

5
00:00:33.286 --> 00:00:38.029
You get to sit around in your pajamas, watching TV and eating your favorite foods.

6
00:00:42.071 --> 00:00:43.532
I'm having an emergency!"

7
00:00:43.992 --> 00:00:44.472
I said.

8
00:00:46.373 --> 00:00:48.154
Molly stopped chewing her donut.

9
00:00:49.215 --> 00:00:50.036
"What's wrong?"

10
00:00:50.496 --> 00:00:51.116
she asked.

11
00:00:51.136 --> 00:00:52.857
"Is somebody sick?"

12
00:00:53.978 --> 00:00:54.758
I shook my head.

13
00:00:54.778 --> 00:00:57.500
"No one is sick—except me.

14
00:00:58.024 --> 00:01:01.227
I'm sick of my cousin, Oliver, and he isn't even here yet!"

15
00:01:02.408 --> 00:01:03.509
Molly looked puzzled.

16
00:01:03.529 --> 00:01:06.132
"Iggy," she said.

17
00:01:06.152 --> 00:01:07.994
"What are you talking about?"

18
00:01:08.014 --> 00:01:12.918
"I'm talking about my bratty cousin, Oliver," I said.

19
00:01:12.938 --> 00:01:16.942
"He's coming to visit, and he's going to share my room!"

20
00:01:19.484 --> 00:01:22.828
I told Molly about Oliver visiting over winter vacation.

21
00:01:24.020 --> 00:01:29.202
"My mom said Aunt Julia and Uncle John want to take a cruise," I added.

22
00:01:29.222 --> 00:01:31.443
"Without Oliver?"

23
00:01:32.003 --> 00:01:32.704
asked Molly.

24
00:01:33.724 --> 00:01:34.244
I nodded.

25
00:01:34.264 --> 00:01:37.326
"My uncle has been working really hard.

26
00:01:38.326 --> 00:01:40.387
They want to take a vacation by themselves."

27
00:01:41.507 --> 00:01:42.368
Molly giggled.

28
00:01:42.388 --> 00:01:48.090
"They probably want to get away from Oliver for a while!"

29
00:01:48.110 --> 00:01:52.212
"I bet you're right," I said glumly.

30
00:01:53.196 --> 00:01:55.438
"But why do they have to leave him with us?"

31
00:01:56.758 --> 00:02:01.241
Just then we heard Josh and Jenny walking up the stairs with their dad.

32
00:02:02.442 --> 00:02:03.823
Molly and I looked down.

33
00:02:05.144 --> 00:02:07.085
They were all carrying grocery bags.

34
00:02:07.105 --> 00:02:09.347
"I've got a problem!"

35
00:02:09.767 --> 00:02:10.487
I burst out.

36
00:02:11.548 --> 00:02:12.529
Josh looked up at me.

37
00:02:12.549 --> 00:02:14.550
"Really?" he said.

38
00:02:14.570 --> 00:02:18.976
"Maybe we'd better have a powwow."

39
00:02:18.996 --> 00:02:23.539
My friends and I have a "powwow" whenever somebody has a big problem.

40
00:02:24.520 --> 00:02:26.541
We get together to figure out a solution.

41
00:02:26.561 --> 00:02:28.602
"That's a great idea!"

42
00:02:28.982 --> 00:02:29.382
I said.

43
00:02:29.402 --> 00:02:32.644
"I'll go get dressed," said Molly.

44
00:02:32.664 --> 00:02:36.587
"A powwow sounds like more fun than a mental health day."

45
00:02:36.607 --> 00:02:40.549
"We'll meet in five minutes outside on the front steps!"

46
00:02:41.049 --> 00:02:41.730
said Josh.

47
00:02:43.571 --> 00:02:45.652
Soon we were all sitting on the front steps.

48
00:02:46.796 --> 00:02:50.457
But it was freezing outside, and an icy rain had started to fall.

49
00:02:50.477 --> 00:02:55.058
"Let's go inside by the radiator," said Jenny.

50
00:02:56.759 --> 00:03:00.020
We went into the front hall and stood by the big radiator.

51
00:03:01.700 --> 00:03:03.641
It was making loud banging noises.

52
00:03:05.381 --> 00:03:07.502
But at least the front hall was warm.

53
00:03:07.522 --> 00:03:11.783
I told Josh and Jenny about Oliver's coming to visit.

54
00:03:11.803 --> 00:03:14.664
"And he's going to share my room!"

55
00:03:15.124 --> 00:03:15.704
I groaned.

56
00:03:16.756 --> 00:03:20.498
"So I won't have any quiet time to work on a new invention.

57
00:03:20.818 --> 00:03:24.239
And I really wanted to get into the Inventor's Hall of Fame!"

58
00:03:24.259 --> 00:03:26.540
"How do you do that?"

59
00:03:27.061 --> 00:03:27.801
asked Josh.

60
00:03:29.041 --> 00:03:32.283
"You have to invent something really amazing," I explained.

61
00:03:32.303 --> 00:03:36.545
"And if you do invent something cool, you win a trophy.

62
00:03:36.965 --> 00:03:41.487
Plus, you get your picture on the Inventor's Hall of Fame website."

63
00:03:42.607 --> 00:03:43.768
Molly's face lit up.

64
00:03:44.664 --> 00:03:46.525
"You would be famous, Iggy!"

65
00:03:46.545 --> 00:03:50.626
"But now Oliver is coming," I said.

66
00:03:50.646 --> 00:03:52.866
"He'll spoil everything!"

67
00:03:52.886 --> 00:03:56.767
"It could be fun," said Josh.

68
00:03:57.868 --> 00:03:59.228
He was trying to cheer me up.

69
00:04:00.288 --> 00:04:02.149
"You'll be like a big brother to Oliver."

70
00:04:02.169 --> 00:04:05.450
"Me, a big brother?"

71
00:04:06.010 --> 00:04:06.490
I said.

72
00:04:07.270 --> 00:04:09.151
I had to admit I hadn't thought of that.

73
00:04:09.171 --> 00:04:14.561
"We could fix him a cute little bed in your room," Jenny chimed in.

74
00:04:14.581 --> 00:04:18.283
"And invent games and fun activities to do!"

75
00:04:18.763 --> 00:04:19.483
added Molly.

76
00:04:20.584 --> 00:04:21.304
I smiled.

77
00:04:21.324 --> 00:04:23.846
"You guys are the best friends ever!"

78
00:04:24.306 --> 00:04:24.766
I said.

79
00:04:24.786 --> 00:04:28.448
I was starting to feel a little better.

80
00:04:29.489 --> 00:04:32.851
Maybe Oliver's visit wouldn't be so bad after all.

81
00:04:33.871 --> 00:04:37.273
I'm glad I didn't have a crystal ball to see the future right then.

82
00:04:38.294 --> 00:04:41.556
Because if I'd had a crystal ball, I would have seen the truth.

83
00:04:42.753 --> 00:04:46.566
Oliver was going to be trouble—big trouble!
